# Production environment variables.
#
# The core experience requires NONE of these. Local development and the test
# suite run with zero configuration: with no DATABASE_URL the application uses an
# embedded PGlite database, and no upstream needs a key.
#
# Only set DATABASE_URL for a real deployment.

# Hosted Postgres connection string.
#
# In production nightglass refuses to start without this rather than silently
# using an embedded database, which would lose every saved plan on the next
# cold start. Locally, leaving it unset selects PGlite.
#
# Neon, Vercel Postgres, Supabase and any other Postgres all work.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# Postgres schema to place nightglass tables in. Defaults to "public".
# Set this when one Postgres instance is shared with another application.
# Must be a plain lowercase identifier: DATABASE_SCHEMA="nightglass"

# Canonical origin, used for metadata, OpenGraph, the sitemap and public/mcp.json.
# Set this to the real production alias after the first deploy so preview
# deployments do not advertise it: SITE_URL="https://nightglass.vercel.app"